{
  "milestone": "08G",
  "phase": 1,
  "title": "Phase 1: Reconcile Milestone 08F Results and Diagnostics",
  "executive_summary": {
    "m3_rmse_discrepancy_resolved": "Historical M3 IID RMSE was ~2.38 K in 08C and ~3.75 K in 08F. The root cause is that evaluate_milestone_08f_multires.py passed hardcoded log_k_mean=0.5, log_k_std=1.0 instead of the checkpoint's fitted values (mean=0.8623669, std=0.4588298). When evaluated with checkpoint fitted stats, M3 achieves 2.319 K at 32x32 and 2.376 K at 256x256, perfectly reproducing the historical ~2.38 K benchmark. Crucially, under canonical normalization, A3 achieves 1.848 K at 32x32 and 1.916 K at 256x256, proving that A3 outperforms M3 even more substantially than previously reported.",
    "a3_latency_discrepancy_resolved": "The 1.3 ms overhead claimed in 08F was measured strictly at 32x32 (8.18 ms vs 6.88 ms). At 256x256, spatial feature grids have 64x more cells (65,536 vs 1,024), causing the 3-layer convolutional refinement block to take ~10.68 ms. Claiming 1.3 ms as a general surrogate overhead was an aggregation error that neglected resolution scaling.",
    "boundary_distance_units_resolved": "The mean distance to boundary of 0.0155 reported in 08F was in physical meters [m] on the unit domain [0, 1]^2. At 256x256, dx = 1/256 = 0.003906 m, meaning 0.0155 m corresponds to ~3.97 grid cells. At 32x32, 0.0155 m is ~0.50 grid cells. The metric was physically consistent in meters, but was ambiguously described without specifying physical meters vs discrete grid units.",
    "independent_cohort_provenance_confirmed": "Checkpoints for A1 and A3 were saved and frozen prior to generating and evaluating independent_cohort_08f.h5. No parameter tuning was performed on the cohort."
  },
